WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.176
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book three.

2
00:00:05.476 --> 00:00:08.770
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:15.263
Unit eight: Competitive Sports. Today you will tell about earlier past actions with the past perfect.

4
00:00:15.563 --> 00:00:18.111
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:22.648
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:24.392
Athlete.

7
00:00:25.383 --> 00:00:27.975
Athlete means a person who is good at sports.

8
00:00:28.583 --> 00:00:30.409
She is a talented athlete.

9
00:00:31.017 --> 00:00:34.087
Your turn. Say: Athlete.

10
00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:37.853
Athlete.

11
00:00:38.617 --> 00:00:39.653
Endurance.

12
00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.938
Endurance means the ability to keep going for a long time.

13
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.689
Marathon runners need endurance.

14
00:00:47.283 --> 00:00:49.645
Your turn. Say: Endurance.

15
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.803
Endurance.

16
00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:55.539
Discipline.

17
00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.722
Discipline means controlling yourself to train regularly.

18
00:01:00.317 --> 00:01:02.235
Discipline makes champions.

19
00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.363
Your turn. Say: Discipline.

20
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:09.166
Discipline.

21
00:01:09.917 --> 00:01:10.720
Rival.

22
00:01:11.717 --> 00:01:14.099
Rival means a person you compete against.

23
00:01:14.683 --> 00:01:16.520
My rival is also my friend.

24
00:01:17.117 --> 00:01:19.595
Your turn. Say: Rival.

25
00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:23.411
Rival.

26
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.430
Personal best.

27
00:01:26.417 --> 00:01:28.776
Personal best means your best result ever.

28
00:01:29.383 --> 00:01:31.464
I ran a new personal best!

29
00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:34.737
Your turn. Say: Personal best.

30
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.787
Personal best.

31
00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:40.702
Training regimen.

32
00:01:41.717 --> 00:01:44.715
Training regimen means a strict plan for exercise.

33
00:01:45.317 --> 00:01:47.665
Her training regimen starts at five a.m.

34
00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.937
Your turn. Say: Training regimen.

35
00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.103
Training regimen.

36
00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:57.130
Perseverance.

37
00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:01.254
Perseverance means continuing even when it is difficult.

38
00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.536
Perseverance helped him win.

39
00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:07.139
Your turn. Say: Perseverance.

40
00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.210
Perseverance.

41
00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:12.951
Setback.

42
00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:16.971
Setback means a problem that slows your progress.

43
00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:19.513
An injury was a big setback.

44
00:02:20.117 --> 00:02:22.676
Your turn. Say: Setback.

45
00:02:25.533 --> 00:02:26.639
Setback.

46
00:02:27.383 --> 00:02:28.373
Comeback.

47
00:02:29.383 --> 00:02:32.254
Comeback means returning to success after a problem.

48
00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:34.896
The team made an amazing comeback.

49
00:02:35.483 --> 00:02:37.857
Your turn. Say: Comeback.

50
00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:41.585
Comeback.

51
00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:43.502
Milestone.

52
00:02:44.517 --> 00:02:47.805
Milestone means an important point in progress.

53
00:02:48.417 --> 00:02:50.521
Her first medal was a milestone.

54
00:02:51.117 --> 00:02:53.641
Your turn. Say: Milestone.

55
00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.140
Milestone.

56
00:02:58.883 --> 00:03:00.372
Sports psychology.

57
00:03:01.383 --> 00:03:04.463
Sports psychology means the study of the mind in sports.

58
00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:07.978
Sports psychology helps athletes stay calm.

59
00:03:08.583 --> 00:03:11.863
Your turn. Say: Sports psychology.

60
00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.293
Sports psychology.

61
00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:18.051
Focus.

62
00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:22.094
Focus means giving all your attention to one thing.

63
00:03:22.683 --> 00:03:24.323
Keep your focus on the ball.

64
00:03:24.917 --> 00:03:27.743
Your turn. Say: Focus.

65
00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:31.531
Focus.

66
00:03:32.333 --> 00:03:36.843
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:39.985
Visal, I heard about your swimming race!

68
00:03:41.083 --> 00:03:44.850
Yes! I swam a new personal best.

69
00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.984
But you were injured last year, right?

70
00:03:49.083 --> 00:03:52.792
Yes. I had hurt my shoulder before the season started.

71
00:03:53.883 --> 00:03:55.453
How did you make a comeback?

72
00:03:56.550 --> 00:04:02.244
I had followed a strict training regimen for months. Perseverance and focus helped me.

73
00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.191
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:08.293
Grammar focus: Past perfect.

75
00:04:08.593 --> 00:04:09.827
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:10.517 --> 00:04:13.236
She had trained hard before the competition began.

77
00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.254
I had hurt my shoulder before the season.

78
00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.660
When I arrived, the race had already started.

79
00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:24.202
Use the past perfect for the earlier of two past actions.

80
00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:29.193
Be careful! Don't say: She has trained hard before the race began.

81
00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:34.433
Say: She had trained hard before the race began.

82
00:04:34.733 --> 00:04:37.186
Use 'had' for the earlier past action.

83
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.525
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:41.333 --> 00:04:42.288
The Comeback.

85
00:04:42.588 --> 00:04:46.410
The athlete had a big setback last year: a knee injury.

86
00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:50.317
She had followed a strict training regimen for months.

87
00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:54.122
Discipline and perseverance built her endurance.

88
00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:57.806
She had trained hard before the competition began.

89
00:04:58.800 --> 00:05:04.004
Thanks to sports psychology and focus, she ran a personal best and beat her rival.

90
00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:08.974
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:09.817 --> 00:05:12.292
She blank trained hard before the race.

92
00:05:12.592 --> 00:05:16.083
A, had. B, has. C, have.

93
00:05:19.633 --> 00:05:21.319
The answer is A: had.

94
00:05:22.483 --> 00:05:25.145
A problem that slows your progress is a blank.

95
00:05:25.445 --> 00:05:29.458
A, setback. B, milestone. C, comeback.

96
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:35.452
The answer is A: setback.

97
00:05:36.617 --> 00:05:39.301
Continuing even when it is difficult is blank.

98
00:05:39.601 --> 00:05:43.719
A, perseverance. B, endurance. C, rivalry.

99
00:05:47.267 --> 00:05:49.591
The answer is A: perseverance.

100
00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:54.010
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:58.173
Describe a time you overcame a setback in sports or study.

102
00:06:06.983 --> 00:06:08.507
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:08.807 --> 00:06:18.126
I failed a maths test last year. I had not studied enough. After that, I practised every day, and I got an A in the final exam.

104
00:06:18.426 --> 00:06:20.309
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:21.217 --> 00:06:25.309
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and past perfect.

106
00:06:25.609 --> 00:06:29.933
Today's value is perseverance. Keep trying, even when it is hard.

107
00:06:30.233 --> 00:06:32.607
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

108
00:06:32.907 --> 00:06:36.105
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

